# Voice performance: the DVTD stationary flow rig on subject 1's /s/ (s1-11-bass-s) at the printed 2.9979 W
#   level: P_sub 2841.4 Pa at the tap; printed comparison values U 0.00105507 m^3/s and SPL 72.1 dB re 20 uPa.
# Card by OliveDove, fric1 (owner order MB 15368; rulings 15490, 15773, 15828, 15902, 16025; NavyTower 15491,
#   15765, 16041). Every number below is read from a cited file; none is fitted to a recording.
#
# SOURCE OF THE RIG: P. Birkholz et al. (2020), Sci. Data 7:255, doi 10.1038/s41597-020-00597-w (CC BY 4.0), and
#   its dataset (the DVTD archive, CC0, figshare 11897187). The printed values and the PSD comparison file are
#   s1-11-bass-s-noise-metadata.txt and s1-11-bass-s-noise-psd.txt of that archive.
# TRACT: s1-11-bass-s-inner-surface-closed.stl cut by the level route (slice3d.py, NavyTower): 96 sections
#   of about 2 mm, glottis first. Section 0 = 1.316450e-04 m^2. Rigid (no tract_wall row): a printed solid.
# FRICATIVE SOURCE: Stevens' printed source at an obstacle (K. N. Stevens, Acoustic Phonetics, Fig. 2.33(a), on
#   Shadle's 1985 data; read on MIT OCW 6.541J handout 03/02/04, p. 6; MB 17645, 17712): in 300 Hz bands
#   L = C(f) + 20 log10(U^3 A^-2.5) - 212 dB re 1 dyn/cm^2, U in cm^3/s and A in cm^2, C(f) the upper curve as
#   digitized in fs-couple's turbulence_noise.rs (0.55-10 kHz). The caption's U^3 rule is used as printed: the
#   figure's own two curves imply U^1.89 to U^2.78, and no exponent is refit. A is the constriction k = 84
#   (1.340011e-05 m^2, the cut's minimum), opening into j = 95 (3.060162e-04 m^2, the largest section between k
#   and the lips, MB 15828), whose Borda-Carnot drop is solved in the glottal junction; seed 1. The source sits
#   at the obstacle m = 90, the junction after section 90, 12.1 mm downstream of k along the cut: the incisors'
#   gap, measured on the same surface as the waist between the cavity behind the teeth and the cavity behind
#   the lips on 9 midsagittal slices (its edges lie in sections 89 to 91, their median in section 90). The
#   figure's rig had one 0.0804 cm^2 constriction, its obstacle 3 cm downstream, a 5.0 cm^2 tube and flows of
#   160 and 420 cm^3/s; this rig's 562 to 959 cm^3/s through 0.134 cm^2 lie above those flows, and its
#   obstacle sits 12.1 mm from the constriction: both gaps are stated on the page.
# GLOTTIS: the model's own adapter hole (the article: a 4 mm ring, inner diameter 10 mm, flush with the glottal
#   plane). The printable file's bore measures 78.050 mm^2 (9.97 mm) over 4.0 mm, the mean of 8
#   plane sections; glottal_orifice takes Ishizaka and Flanagan (1972) eq 6 recovery into section 0, N = 0.5929
#   (MB 16025). The fold rows are unread (the grammar needs them; glottal_orifice replaces the folds).
# SUBGLOTTAL TUBE, glottis end first, from the printed misc parts by plane sections: the 4.0 mm hole; trachea.stl's
#   bore, 253.852 mm^2 (18 mm), 82.0 mm (its 5.0 mm spigot fills the horn's 5.0 mm thread socket);
#   bronchial_horn.stl's bore from the socket floor down 17 slices of 2.0 mm, each at its midpoint's area,
#   to 120.0 mm below the glottal plane, the article's pressure tap (no tap port is in either printed part). The
#   article's 18 to 10 mm taper is in no printed part; the card follows the files (MB 15828). Below the tap the
#   horn and the tank are replaced by the held pressure.
# SUBGLOTTAL PRESSURE: the printed P_sub, held at the tube's far end (the tap). The 0.1 s ramp is authored and
#   lies before the reads (the last 2 s).
# AMBIENT: 22 C, 1007 hPa, 46 % relative humidity, as the article prints for the anechoic chamber.
# TERMINATION: the Levine-Schwinger exact unflanged thin-wall load, 256 quadrature nodes (MB 15902). The printed
#   wall is 4 mm thick: the real load lies between the unflanged and flanged limits.
# RECEIVER: the mouth flow as a free-field monopole at the rig microphone, 0.30 m in front of and 0.30 m beside the
#   mouth (0.424 m), as the article prints; the 45-degree directivity is not modelled.
# AUDIO: 40 kHz (MB 15902), 3.0 s, one mechanics step per output sample.
frankensim-voice-performance-v1
audio 40000 120000 1
full_scale_pa 1.0
ambient moist_air 295.15 100700 0.46
fold two_mass 1.25e-4 2.5e-5 80 8 25 0.1 3.57e-4 1.4e-2 2.5e-3
fold_damping_upper 0.6
termination unflanged_thin_wall 256
tract_source dvtd-2020-s1-11-bass-s-inner-surface-closed-level-cut
tract_licence DVTD archive CC0 (figshare 11897187); article CC BY 4.0, doi 10.1038/s41597-020-00597-w
